{"type":"message","id":"944ab4fd","parentId":"080ee2ee","timestamp":"2026-05-17T03:02:30.382Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The connection works. The issue is likely that the Workers platform itself is returning error 1101 (which is typically a Workers specific error). This might mean the route/script has an issue or the request format is not quite right.\n\nLet me try with GET to see if it works, or check available routes.\n\nActually wait - for POST /send, the issue could be that the `send` endpoint requires different parameters. Let me try a simpler approach - maybe the API is using a different key header format.\n\nActually, looking at the history calls working with `X-API-Key`, but POST failing with 1101... Error 1101 from Cloudflare Workers typically means \"Worker threw an exception\" or \"Script thrown an unhandled exception\". \n\nThe script itself might be crashing when it tries to process the POST request, so there could be a bug in how it's validating or handling the send endpoint.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-971f8281-31b3-441a-b6a3-a9d55358ed0e","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-f5b9de0b-f44e-4496-8b5f-ce0dcc6d9fde","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/health\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":8322,"output":276,"cacheRead":11392,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19990,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778986943237,"responseId":"chatcmpl-8c71215f-79ee-44d4-a6c0-6d0cc2385ac8"}}
